# The trial of pod-egress part 3 in podssh (T-035; calls C631 to C634), at
# podssh's main 2ffb7cd7 (pod-egress-part3.commit), after the trial of part
# 1 (pod-egress-part3.needs). podssh-ws's eice/ and iap/ become modules of
# glue over pod-egress (pub use pod_egress::ROAD::*, and podssh's way out
# for a ProxyChoice: eice::connect, iap::connect, each USER_AGENT;
# iap::carry::{Say, Line, note, open}, which say the carrier's events as
# podssh's lines), so that podssh-cli does not change. The unit tests of
# eice/ and iap/ leave podssh with them. Each podcrates tag moves to
# v0.52.0. The steps: the record with its citations, the repository checks;
# no moved file stays; pod-egress in the tree with eice and iap; clippy and
# the tests of podssh-ws with each feature; clippy of the CLI; the CLI's
# unit tests of the clouds' roads and its tests of EICE and IAP through the
# stand-in proxy; rustfmt of the changed crates; each Rust toolchain of the
# workflows against the rust-version of podcrates; each test target that
# the gate names.
cargo run -q -p podssh-todo -- remap Cargo.lock > /dev/null
cargo run -q -p podssh-todo -- check
python3 scripts/check-repo.py
test ! -e crates/podssh-ws/src/eice && test ! -e crates/podssh-ws/src/iap
cargo tree -q -p podssh-ws -i pod-egress -e features | grep -q 'pod-egress feature "iap"'
cargo tree -q -p podssh-ws -i pod-egress -e features | grep -q 'pod-egress feature "eice"'
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podssh-ws --all-features -- -D warnings -A clippy::collapsible_if
cargo test -q -p podssh-ws --all-features
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podssh-cli -- -D warnings -A clippy::collapsible_if
cargo test -q -p podssh-cli --lib -- ssh::cloud cp::link
cargo test -q -p podssh-cli --test iap_cli --test eice_cli
cargo fmt -p podssh-ws -p podssh-cli --check
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-tests.py"
